<http://purl.org/nanopub/temp/np1/assertion> {
  <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/organism-blueprint-cattle> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/Claim> .
  <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/organism-blueprint-cattle> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Proposed anatomical blueprint for \"cattle\": 13 organ systems, 67 organs, 280 tissues and 369 cell types that Uberon and the Cell Ontology record for Bos taurus." .
  <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/organism-blueprint-cattle> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/description> "The description \"cattle\" was resolved to Bos taurus (NCBITaxon:9913), most specific of the taxon words found (subclass of the others). From that taxon the tool proposes a body > organ system > organ > tissue > cell hierarchy of existing ontology terms: 13 organ systems, 67 organs, 280 tissues and 369 cell types. Of the 67 organs, 62 carry a taxon basis stated by the ontology for this taxon or an ancestor, 2 are stated only for all animals, and 3 are merely not excluded. This is a proposal assembled from ontology statements. It is not an observation of any organism, and no specimen, image or measurement enters it." .
  <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/organism-blueprint-cattle> <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/hypothesisType> "ontology-derived design proposal" .
  <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/organism-blueprint-cattle> <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/context> "Taxon Bos taurus (NCBITaxon:9913), verified live as the most specific of the taxon words found. Selection: organ systems are subclasses of \"anatomical system\" in Uberon's core subsets, most general kept; organs are parts of a system in the major_organ, organ_slim, efo_slim or vertebrate_core subsets, ranked major organs first then by the number of cell types the Cell Ontology records for them, at most 6 per system; at most 6 tissues and 8 cell types per organ. Taxon filter: a structure is dropped when Uberon or the Cell Ontology states never_in_taxon on the term, a superclass, or a whole it is part of, for a taxon containing this one, or states in_taxon for a taxon unrelated to this one; for non-vertebrates the vertebrate_core subset is dropped as well. Absence of a constraint is not presence, which is why every organ carries its taxon evidence. Retrieved from Ubergraph on 2026-10-31T06:47:04.325Z; the cache pins the bytes. Unknown stays unknown: nothing was filled in where the ontologies are silent." .
  <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/organism-blueprint-cattle> <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/hasEvidence> <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/organism-blueprint-cattle-queries> .
  <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/organism-blueprint-cattle> <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/proposedTest> "Take a curated anatomical atlas for Bos taurus that was not used here, and count two things: structures the atlas lists at organ level that this blueprint omits, and organs this blueprint proposes that the atlas does not record for the taxon. A blueprint whose \"stated\" organs disagree with the atlas would falsify the selection rule; disagreement confined to the \"not excluded\" organs would instead show the ontology's taxon constraints are too sparse, which is the limit already recorded here." .
  <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/organism-blueprint-cattle> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Does not establish: that an individual of Bos taurus has these structures, that the list is complete, or that any part of it was measured. Uberon's taxon constraints are sparse, so organs marked \"not excluded\" may be absent in the organism; tissues and cell types are ontology part_of statements, not counts from a specimen. Nothing here is a genome, and no function is predicted." .
  <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/organism-blueprint-cattle> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#seeAlso> <https://github.com/fractastical/delphi/blob/main/organism-design/examples/cattle.json> .
}
<http://purl.org/nanopub/temp/np1/provenance> {
  <http://purl.org/nanopub/temp/np1/assertion> <http://www.w3.org/ns/prov#wasAttributedTo> <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/agent/delphisci-organism-blueprint-tool> .
  <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/agent/delphisci-organism-blueprint-tool> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/ns/prov#SoftwareAgent> .
  <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/agent/delphisci-organism-blueprint-tool> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "organism-design/blueprint.mjs: a deterministic Node script that reads a description with hand-written word lists and queries Ubergraph. No language model is in the loop." .
  <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/agent/delphisci-organism-blueprint-tool> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/identifier> "organism-design/blueprint.mjs" .
  <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/agent/delphisci-organism-blueprint-tool> <https://schema.org/codeRepository> <https://github.com/fractastical/delphi> .
}
<http://purl.org/nanopub/temp/np1/pubinfo> {
  <http://purl.org/nanopub/temp/np1/> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/created> "2026-10-31T14:15:32.077Z"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime> .
  <http://purl.org/nanopub/temp/np1/> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/creator> <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/agent/delphisci-organism-blueprint-tool> .
  <http://purl.org/nanopub/temp/np1/> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Proposed anatomical blueprint for \"cattle\": 13 organ systems, 67 organs, 280 tissues and 369 cell types that Uberon and the Cell Ontology record for Bos taurus." .
  <http://purl.org/nanopub/temp/np1/> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/license> <https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/> .
  <http://purl.org/nanopub/temp/np1/> <http://purl.org/nanopub/x/hasNanopubType> <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/Claim> .
  <http://purl.org/nanopub/temp/np1/> <http://purl.org/nanopub/x/introduces> <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/organism-blueprint-cattle> .
  <http://purl.org/nanopub/temp/np1/> <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/domain> <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/domain/https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/domain/organism-anatomy-blueprints-from-ontologies> .
  <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/domain/https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/domain/organism-anatomy-blueprints-from-ontologies> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/domain/organism-anatomy-blueprints-from-ontologies" .
  <http://purl.org/nanopub/temp/np1/> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "No assertion, provenance or pubinfo template is declared. The pipeline maps each Project Delphi v2.0 class to the published ProbKnow template for that class, and those published templates still use legacy probknow terms, so a v2.0 record cannot instantiate them: check-nanopub-conformance.py reports every assertion triple unmatched and the required statement missing. Migrated templates exist in the ontology source but have not been republished; see the record delphir:claim/delphi-v2-template-declarations-are-false for the counts and the options." .
  <http://purl.org/nanopub/temp/np1/> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Owner ORCID not set: no human is named in this draft. The key owner passes --owner <orcid IRI> to organism-design/nanopubs/build.mjs at signing time, and that one value populates dct:creator and prov:actedOnBehalfOf." .
}
